{
  "dom_id": "step-q97785",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "The graph of $y=f(-2x)-1,$ can be obtained from the graph of $y=f(x)$ by applying **some** of the following transformations:\n\n- $(\\text{T}1)$ - Reflection across the $x$-axis\n\n- $(\\text{T}2)$ - Translation by $1$ unit down\n\n- $(\\text{T}3)$ - Reflection across the $y$-axis\n\n- $(\\text{T}4)$ - Stretch of scale factor $\\frac{1}{2}$ parallel to the $x$-axis\n\nWhich of the following could be a possible ordering of the appropriate transformations?",
